<title>ITALY: Generali forms Brazilian joint venture.</title>
<headline>Generali forms Brazilian joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian company Generali do Brasil Sa, controlled by Italy's giant insurer Generali, said it had formed a joint venture to market life insurance and pensions with the Banco Sudameris in Brazil.</p>
<p>Banco Sudameris is controlled by Italian bank Banca Commerciale Italiana (BCI).</p>
<p>The new venture to be called Sudameris Generali Companhia Nacional de Seguros SA will market the products through the 180 Brazilian branches of Sudameris.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
